Drops store_state's check that a published state owes no fdatasync, so a
state making sync = true writes visible before they are durable is published.
Guarded-by: "pipeline: publishing a state that owes an fdatasync degrades the engine"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm b/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
index d3f22be..47bd8b7 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
+++ b/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
@@ -4953,7 +4953,7 @@ void DB::store_state(const std::shared_ptr<const EngineState> &old_state,
   }
   // Durability before visibility: a published state never contains a
   // sync=true write that fdatasync has not confirmed.
-  if (new_state->sync_requested_seq > new_state->durable_seq) {
+  if (false) {
     deem_as_degraded(std::format(
         "invariant violation: publishing sync_requested_seq {} above "
         "durable_seq {}",
